          "source_quote": "ὡς παρ’ ἰδίων γνώμην εἰληφὼς ὑποστέλλεσθαι ἔγνω",
          "english_quote": "he received the information as though from his own people and decided to withdraw.",
          "issue": "In this receive-from construction, γνώμη naturally supports counsel, advice, or judgment. Rendering it as 'information' obscures the distinction between hearing the report and receiving what he regarded as counsel from his own people. The note does not preserve the material 'advice' alternative.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider 'having received what he took to be advice from his own people, he decided to withdraw.' Revise the note to compare advice/counsel with the broader information reading and explain the selection. The replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὑπολῆσαι",
          "english_quote": "The selected reading is lexically unusual in this construction and may reflect loss of ξ from a form of ὑπολήγω, “abate” or “cease.”",
          "issue": "The proposed reading ὑπολῆξαι differs from the supplied ὑπολῆσαι by replacing σ with ξ, not simply by restoring an omitted ξ. The note's account of the proposed change is inaccurate. The verified printed reading must remain distinguished from the conjectural regularization.",
          "suggested_revision": "State: 'The edition reads ὑπολῆσαι. A possible regularization is ὑπολῆξαι, with ξ instead of σ, understood as “cease” or “abate.” That regularization is conjectural; the English follows a contextual interpretation of the printed wording.' Do not claim new print or manuscript verification.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
