          "english_quote": "Thinking that Caesar was seeking him for harm",
          "issue": "Taking Caesar as the subject of ζητεῖν is contextually defensible, but the supplied Καίσαρος is genitive, rather than the accusative ordinarily expected for that subject in the infinitival construction after νομίσας. The draft silently passes over this printed grammatical irregularity. It is not an unverified OCR reading and does not by itself require blocking publication.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the contextual English but add a source-quoted note explaining that the edition prints Καίσαρος and that Caesar is understood as the subject of ζητεῖν despite the irregular case. If Καίσαρα is mentioned, label it explicitly as a proposed grammatical regularization, not the supplied reading.",
